# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SmazkaVG v1.2 — Anime Eyelash Example
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Demonstrates:
#   1. Cubic Bézier edges (curved, not straight segments)
#   2. Variable-width stroke profiles (tapered "power stroke")
#   3. Split namespace: s (structural), a (assertions), c (constraints), p (paint)
#   4. Convex QP only (termination guaranteed)
#   5. Labeled node fields
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Vertices ──────────────────────────────────────────────
v 0 0 0              # Base of lash (inner corner)
v 1 100 0            # Base of lash (outer corner)
v 2 50 20            # Midpoint (for topology)

# ── Edges (CUBIC BÉZIER) ──────────────────────────────────
# Main lash: curved upward, cubic Bézier with two control points
e 0 0 1 type=cubic 30 -40 70 -40
# Lower lid: gentle curve downward
e 1 0 1 type=cubic 30 10 70 10

# ── Faces ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (No face here - the two edges share endpoints, not a closed region)
# See triangle.smazka for face examples

# ── Strokes (VARIABLE-WIDTH TAPER PROFILES) ───────────────
# Upper lash: thick in middle, tapered at ends (5 samples)
#   t=0.0: 1.0px, t=0.25: 3.0px, t=0.5: 4.5px, t=0.75: 3.0px, t=1.0: 1.5px
s 0 0 1A1A1AFF 1.0 3.0 4.5 3.0 1.5

# ── Structural (s) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Group the eye components
s 0 group_id 0 1     # v0 in group 1 (eye)
s 1 group_id 1 1     # v1 in group 1
s 2 group_id 2 1     # v2 in group 1

# ── Assertions (a) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Validate topology (redundant but explicit)
a 0 edge_connects 0 0 1   # e0 connects v0→v1
a 1 edge_connects 1 0 1   # e1 connects v0→v1

# ── Constraints (c) — LP/QP only, convex ─────────────────
# Bounding box (LP)
c 0 bbox_clamp 0 -10 -50 110 50    # v0 must stay in box
c 1 bbox_clamp 1 -10 -50 110 50    # v1 must stay in box

# Minimum distance between lash and lid (LP)
c 2 min_dist 0 1 5.0               # e0 and e1 must be ≥5px apart

# ── Paint (p) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Diffusion curve along the lower lid (subtle shading)
p 0 diffusion 1 L FFE0D0 R 4A3020  # Warm skin tone → dark shadow
